Oauth2

Debrid-Link use the Oauth2 specification (RFC 6749). https://oauth.net/2/

The Oauth2 endpoint is: https://debrid-link.com/api/oauth
The Oauth2 authorization endpoint is: https://debrid-link.com/oauth/auth
You must create an app to generate a client_id and client_secret from your account to use our API.
Oauth success result

The HTTP status code is in the 200 range.

{
  "access_token": "",
  "...": "..."
}

Oauth error result

The HTTP status code is in the 400/500 ranges.
API return the error code.

{
  "error": "invalid_request"
}

Grant Types

We support this following Grant Types:

    authorization_code: Mobile, Desktop Apps.
    urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:device_code: Limited input capabilities, TV for example.
    password: Username/Password (Not recommended because a captcha and other errors can occur).
    refresh_token: Refresh the access_token.

Scope

The scope syntax is the HTTP verbs and the service separted by dots. Bellow the list of all allowed scopes:

    get.post.delete.downloader
    get.post.delete.seedbox
    get.account
    get.files
    get.post.stream

For example, if you only need to generate downloader links and get user infos you can set the scope value to post.downloader get.user

The default scope value is: get.post.downloader get.post.seedbox get.account
Calling Debrid-Link APIs

For each request that require an authentification, you should send the Authorization: Bearer HTTP header might look like the following.

GET https://debrid-link.com/api/v2/downloader/list
Authorization: Bearer ACCESS_TOKEN

Or using the access_token query string parameter: (Not recommended)

GET /downloader/list?access_token=ACCESS_TOKEN

Authorization flow for browser devices

    1) Redirect the user to the authorization endpoint. Parameters infos

    GET https://debrid-link.com/oauth/auth?
    client_id=CLIENT_ID
    &response_type=code
    &redirect_uri=http%3A%2F%2Flocalhost
    &scope=get.post.downloader%20get.post.seedbox%20get.account
    &state=PASSTHROUG_VALUE (Recommended)
    &code_challenge=code_challenge (Recommended for private app, required for public app)
    &code_challenge_method=S256 (Recommended for private app, required for public app)

    2) User authorize access and will be redirect to the redirect_uri with the error or code field.

    http://localhost#code=AUTHORIZATION_CODE&state=PASSTHROUG_VALUE

    http://localhost#error=ERROR_CODE&state=PASSTHROUG_VALUE

    Compare the state value with the value given in the step 1 if defined.

    3) You create the access_token and the refresh_token with the /token endpoint. Parameters infos
    You MUST send the client_secret or/and code_verifier. The client_secret MUST ONLY BE used on server side. (private app)

    POST https://debrid-link.com/api/oauth/token
    Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

    client_id=CLIENT_ID
    &grant_type=authorization_code
    &code=AUTHORIZATION_CODE
    &client_secret=CLIENT_SECRET (Required if 'code_challenge' not used at step 1)
    &code_verifier=CODE_VERIFIER (Required if 'code_challenge' set at step 1)

    Result

    {
      "access_token": "access_token-value",
      "refresh_token": "refresh_token-value",
      "expires_in": 86400,
      "type": "bearer"
    }

    Read how to handle expired access_token and refresh it

Authorization flow for limited input capabilities devices

    1) Create the device_code. Parameters infos

    POST https://debrid-link.com/api/oauth/device/code
    Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

    client_id=CLIENT_ID
    &scope=get.post.downloader%20get.post.seedbox%20get.account

    Result

    {
      "device_code": "TheDeviceCode",
      "user_code": "ABCD-1234",
      "verification_url": "https://debrid-link.fr/device",
      "expires_in": 900,
      "interval": 3
    }

    2) You notifiy the user to authorize the device on the verification_url by submiting the user_code code.

    QRCode: To make it easier for users to access the verification_url with the user_code pre-filled, you may want to display a QR code. The QR code should encode the verification_url and appends the user_code. Example: https://debrid-link.com/device/ABCD-1234

    3) In background, you poll the API server to get access_token and refresh_token with the /token endpoint.
    Poll the server while the error is authorization_pending.
    The interval specifies the amount of time (in seconds) to wait between requests.
    When success, server will return the access_token, refresh_token, expires_in, token_type.

    POST https://debrid-link.com/api/oauth/token
    Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

    client_id=CLIENT_ID
    &code=DEVICE_CODE
    &grant_type=http%3A%2F%2Foauth.net%2Fgrant_type%2Fdevice%2F1.0

    Result

    {
      "access_token": "access_token-value",
      "refresh_token": "refresh_token-value",
      "expires_in": 86400,
      "type": "bearer"
    }

    Read how to handle expired access_token and refresh it

Authorization flow for password

Only use this method if you can't use another one. A captcha and multiple other errors can occurs.

You create the access_token and the refresh_token with the /token endpoint.

POST https://debrid-link.com/api/oauth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=CLIENT_ID
&grant_type=password
&username=USERNAME
&password=PASSWORD

Result

{
  "access_token": "access_token-value",
  "refresh_token": "refresh_token-value",
  "expires_in": 86400,
  "type": "bearer"
}

Refresh access_token
Increment access_token life for your App

To ease the implementation of the Oauth you can increment the access_token life in the App settings to avoid handle its expiration. Some restrictions when its expiration is greater than 1 day:

    access_token must only be sent in the headers.
    The User-Agent must match the User-Agent that granted this access_token. (It can have different version).

Refresh access_token

You can refresh the access_token without prompting the user for permission when the API return the error badToken or before it expire expire_in.

Refresh the access_token only when it's required. If you call this endpoint too many times, Client and/or User will be blocked by the API rate limits.

Only one access_token per authorization is allowed, so the old access_token will be automatically revoked when a new one is created. For this reason, you must be carefull with async app that can infinite loop the refresh_token.

If the refresh token not return a new access_token, the authorization for your app has expired or revoked. You must restart the authorization flow.

POST https://debrid-link.com/api/oauth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=CLIENT_ID
&refresh_token=REFRESH_TOKEN
&grant_type=refresh_token

Result

{
  "access_token": "access_token-value",
  "expires_in": 86400,
  "type": "bearer"
}

Revoke token

The token can be an access_token or a refresh_token(Recommended).

POST https://debrid-link.com/api/oauth/revoke?token=ACCESS_TOKEN_OR_REFRESH_TOKEN

